t": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy - rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api began failing health checks after the v2.3.1 production deploy (error rate 0.18, unhealthy in all regions). v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy in production, so I rolled back to v2.3.0. The first rollback attempt halted with a partial failure after us-east (orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions); I retried the same rollback, which completed. Current state: us-east, us-west and eu-west all on v2.3.0, healthy=true, error rate 0.002. v2.3.1 remains unhealthy in production and should not be redeployed until fixed. Follow-up: investigate the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-sev2-rollback-v2.3.0-2025"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.3.0 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.002, down from 0.18.\n\n- **Rollback target:** v2.3.0 was the most recent production release marked healthy. v2.3.1 was unhealthy in production, and v2.3.1-rc had only run in staging.\n- **Partial failure:** The first rollback halted after us-east with an orchestrator error, leaving the service mixed across regions. I retried the same rollback to v2.3.0, and it completed.\n- **Incident:** I opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api, which paged on-call. The first create request timed out, so I retried it with an idempotency key. The incident was created once.\n\nv2.3.1 is still unhealthy in production, so it should not be redeployed until it is fixed. The follow-up items are the v2.3.1 failure and the orchestrator partial failure, both noted in the incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}